With the aid of an example, explain the meaning of each of the terms:

(i) Functional energy sources;

(ii) Secondary energy sources *[4 marks]*

Natural uranium contains $0.7\ \%$ Uranium - 235. When Uranium - 235 atom undergoes fission, $200\ \mathrm{MeV}$ of energy is released. Calculate:

(i) the number of U - 235 nuclei contained in $1.00\ \mathrm{kg}$ of natural uranium;

(ii) the cost to be paid to an Electricity company such as ENEO, if electrical energy is sold at the rate of $60$ frs per unit when the U - 235 content in $1.00\ \mathrm{kg}$ completely undergoes fission and all the energy released is converted to electrical energy. *[4 marks]*
